Package: easeling
Type: Package
Title: Minimal 'DrawingML' Graphics Device for 'openxlsx2'
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
  person("Jan Marvin", "Garbuszus", email = "jan.garbuszus@ruhr-uni-bochum.de", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: A base R graphics device that writes plots directly as
    'OOXML' 'DrawingML' vector shapes (ECMA-376,
    <https://ecma-international.org/publications-and-standards/standards/ecma-376/>),
    for adding editable graphics to spreadsheets with
    'openxlsx2' (via its wb_add_drawing() function). Has no dependency on
    'cairo', 'FreeType', 'fontconfig', or 'xml2'; real font metrics are
    used when the 'systemfonts' package is available.
URL: https://github.com/JanMarvin/easeling
BugReports: https://github.com/JanMarvin/easeling/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
NeedsCompilation: yes
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
Suggests: 
  openxlsx2,
  systemfonts,
  testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
